"""The live updates of the records (ADR 0051): the changes as server-sent events.

{{ ("A create, a change, and a delete of a record of a live entity give an event after the commit of the transaction. Listeners of the sessions find the changes when a session writes them to the database, so that the generated and the custom operations both give the events. `GET /live` sends the events to the users that may read the records: " ~ readers ~ ". An event has the entity and the ID of the record, but no values: a client reads the record again.") | wordwrap(72, break_long_words=False) }}

With the setting `LIVE_EVENTS_URL`, the processes send the events
through Redis, so that each replica gets the events of all replicas.
Without it, each process sends only its own events.
{% if presences %}

The broker also keeps the signed-in users on the pages of the records
(ADR 0052). A page notes its user each few seconds, and the broker
forgets a user after PRESENCE_SECONDS without a call. A change of the
users on a record gives the event `presence` to the other users on it.
With Redis, the calls of the pages go through the channel too.
{% endif %}
"""

